cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Variant-level concordance can overstate exact peptide–HLA shortlist reproducibility: a 63-condition HCC1395 audit"
authors:
  - family-names: Yoo
    given-names: Byungwoong
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Seoul, Republic of Korea"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-1797-3100"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ByungwoongYoo/target-stability"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility software and frozen analytical artifacts for a 63-condition
  HCC1395/HCC1395BL SEQC2 audit of computational neoantigen shortlist
  stability. The release evaluates analytical concordance at variant,
  peptide, and exact variant–peptide–HLA resolution. It nominates no biological
  candidate and does not establish presentation, immunogenicity, efficacy,
  safety, treatment benefit, or clinical utility.
keywords:
  - analytical reproducibility
  - neoantigen prioritization
  - peptide-HLA
  - HLA provenance
  - HCC1395
  - SEQC2
  - bioinformatics
  - research software
